name issue_12_lossbwe_policer
describe Policer: 1.5 Mbps enforced by dropping, no queueing (queue=5ms); the loss-based estimate must keep backing off (#12)
# LossBasedBweV2 as libwebrtc ships it (cc v2): loss above the inherent level at a rate above the
# loss-limited bandwidth limits the target; the instant upper bound is 100 kbps / (loss - 5 %).
cc v2
duration 40s
at 0s capacity=1500kbps delay=30ms queue=5ms
# 5 seeds (cc v2): net.loss_pct 7.7-9.9, freeze_total_ms 0-764, target 400-412 kbps. `cc v1`: loss 19.8-25.0, freezes 1.0-1.6 s.
# Was < 12. Owner plan on PR #216 (program.md 0.2, 2026-10-20 22:07 UTC): just above libwebrtc's worst seed in 1-10.
# libwebrtc seeds 1-10: 12.22 8.41 9.95 15.97 10.58 10.84 11.68 11.90 12.11 11.83 (mean 11.55); ours seed 1 13.18 (timing v2).
expect net.loss_pct < 16
# Was < 1500, then < 2500 (Owner sign-off on PR #186, 18:37 UTC, with timing v1). Owner plan on PR #216 (2026-10-20 22:07 UTC):
# just above libwebrtc's worst seed in 1-10, since timing v2 shows the late frames timing v1 dropped.
# libwebrtc seeds 1-10: 14858 11261 10103 10185 5748 5319 14496 15854 9140 9666 (mean 10663); ours seed 1 4685.
expect video.freeze_total_ms < 16000
expect audio.interruptions <= 3
